{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you did not believe in Him.</b> In the commandments of the heart. <b>And you did not hearken to His voice.</b> In the commandments of deed." "<b>And it is possible</b> that ולא האמנתם לו alludes to the Name, the distinct one; and for this reason it did not say of it, following the customary usage of verses in the language of faith, which is construed with ב, in the manner of (Numbers 20:12) ״יען לא האמנתם בי״, and likewise (Exodus 14:31) ״ויאמינו בה׳ ובמשה עבדו״, and likewise (Deuteronomy 1:32) ״ובדבר הזה אינכם מאמינים בה׳ אלהיכם״, and many like these — for had it said of it ב, it would not have been necessary to write ולא שמעתם בקולו, for בו is explained as 'in His name,' and His voice is His name. Therefore it was necessary to say לו in order that the verse mention His great name and remembrance. And the sense of the verse will be: ״ותמרו את פי ה׳ אלהיכם ולא האמנתם לו״ — He is ה׳ אלהיכם; ״ולא שמעתם בקולו״ — He is פי ה׳ אלהיכם. And understand this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:08.473335485Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}